# Coding Standards for Escape Room Project

## TypeScript & React Guidelines

- Use TypeScript-first approach with strict mode enabled
- Prefer React Server Components unless client state is required (`'use client'`)
- Use functional components with hooks over class components
- Import shared modules through `@/` alias instead of relative paths

## Code Style & Formatting

- Use tabs for indentation in UI files (preserve existing style)
- Follow the existing `.cursorrules` guidelines for minimal code changes
- Use early returns to avoid nested conditions
- Prefer descriptive names with "handle" prefix for event handlers
- Use constants over functions where possible

## Component Organization

- Components use PascalCase naming
- Hooks use camelCase naming
- Colocate related styles via Tailwind utility classes or `globals.css`
- Order functions with composing functions appearing earlier in files

## State Management

- Use Zustand store in [src/store/gameStore.ts](mdc:src/store/gameStore.ts) for global game state
- Local component state for UI-only state
- Persist critical state to localStorage for session recovery

## Error Handling

- Add TODO comments for bugs or suboptimal code
- Include proper error boundaries for React components
- Handle async operations with proper error states
